			<div class="content" id="post-content-2027530">
									

<p>I liked this one a lot. I thought that the crazy luxury items were clever, the weirdly-similar but not quite employees were a nice touch, and overall it was something kind of unusual while still fitting into the mainlist landscape. I was all set to upvote.</p>
<p>Then I hit the logs.</p>
<p>The first one was sort of irritating, but I stayed my urge to downvote; it <em>did</em> convey the whole information-gathering side of the skip, so it did have a reason to be there. I didn't care for the &quot;hey man&quot; tone of the person being interviewed, but I suppose there are people who do talk like that, though it all still came off as fairly unnatural.</p>
<p>The second one, as people above have said, just kills this. Silly pulp magazine time traveling gangsters with a tendency to reveal all of the stuff they're doing in tidy, concise conversations. Any mystery that the skip had was neatly excised and replaced with a cheeseball future. It wrecked the reading experience to the point where I had to downvote.</p>

							</div>

								
					
